{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan","id":1212902,"title":"Synergys of The Black Veiled Courtesan?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-28T20:07:46-07:00","id":1212902,"title":"Synergys of The Black Veiled Courtesan?","content":"With the release of White Veil, new synergies exist for Martial Arts characters. For Solaroids, what are the new synergies in Black Claw, Dreaming Pearl Courtesan, White Veil, and social charms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T20:29:55-07:00","id":1212907,"title":"","content":"I thoguht we all agreed not to use the term &quot;Solaroid&quot; anymore","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T20:36:15-07:00","id":1212910,"title":"","content":"I wasn\u2019t aware this was an agreed upon thing. Do you have a thought about the subject of synergies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T20:41:15-07:00","id":1212912,"title":"","content":"Synergy wise (I'm basing this off a Solar Exalted, as I haven't had time to digest the DB charmset), the most obvious is Birdsong Over Blades + Flexing the Emerald Claw, for a poison Decisive effect that is penalized extremely harshly (Manipulation 5 = -5 dice on your resistance roll against poison) that doesn't reset you to base initiative, but also doesn't do any other damage. <br /> <br /> Its low Essence, cheap and cheerful, more for the -2 to all rolls debilitation than the 2i/turn damage, methinks though. <br /> <br /> However, The Solar Charmset is quite weak in terms of generating poison effects, Snake style has one deep in the style, but that one requires dealing damage unfortunately. <br /> <br /> Blithe Unruffled Plumage is pretty sweet and provides the soak that Black Claw lacked (yay, no more dipping into Gazellecarp!), presumably the Soak/Hardness stacks with the Silken Armor artifact? (since it says adds/gains? Hmmm, something to ask the Devs)<br /> <br /> Blinded by laughter is pretty nasty all by itself. I wonder how well it works along with Heart Ripping Claw for the ultimate in Social Combat -&gt; Combat Combat alpha strike?<br /> <br /> I think perhaps what pulls it together is all the Guile effects in White Veil and the fact that you can use it to No-sell attacks with Doe Eyes Defence from Black Claw. Maybe this is the true synergy of the two styles?<br /> <br /> Still searching for more synergies, perhaps what I should be looking for is charms in other sets that impose gnarly conditions but have crap damage to use with Birdsong over Blades...?<br /> <br /> Edit: Hmm, Open Plam Carress at Mastery probably pips Blinded by Laughter for the Ambush game. Disappointing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T20:46:15-07:00","id":1212914,"title":"","content":"If you were desperate, I suppose you could go scrounging around in the Venemous mutation for bennies, but the rules on it are somewhat restrictive. And it\u2019s potency is the same as that of Flexing the Emerald Claw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T22:16:56-07:00","id":1212939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1212907#post1212907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thoguht we all agreed not to use the term &quot;Solaroid&quot; anymore</div> </div> </div> </div>No one came up with anything better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T23:18:29-07:00","id":1212955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1212939#post1212939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one came up with anything better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do they need to? Can't people just say, &quot;Solars and Abyssals?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T23:30:11-07:00","id":1212960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1212955#post1212955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do they need to? Can't people just say, &quot;Solars and Abyssals?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>People want to say or write one word rather than three whenever possible, and also the category includes Infernals, who should likewise be accessing Mastery level effects and casting Solar Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T23:44:55-07:00","id":1212962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1212955#post1212955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do they need to? Can't people just say, &amp;quot;Solars and Abyssals?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that did include I fernals too<br /> <br /> I thoyght Solar or Royal Tier Exalts was good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T03:28:55-07:00","id":1212985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1212960#post1212960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People want to say or write one word rather than three whenever possible\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the posts I've seen on this board, I'm inclined to disagree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1212960#post1212960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and also the category includes Infernals, who should likewise be accessing Mastery level effects and casting Solar Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>So aside from having Mastery*, which Sidereals can also access, what is it that Solars, Abyssals, and Green Sun Princes have in common? Not sorcery (as Abyssals don't have access to the Adamant Circle), not Evocations (as Abyssals are only Resonant with soulsteel), and not Charm design (with Abyssals and Green Sun Princes branching off into Deathlord/shintai directions respectively). It sure isn't in how they're Chosen. Sure, you could say they're all monstrously powerful, but the same is true of Exalted in general.<br /> <br /> Simply put, &quot;Solaroid&quot; is not a good term because the thing it's trying to convey - that you can just lump them all together under the same umbrella - is not a good idea. <br /> <br /> ______________<br /> *Which is not something I've heard, mind. Just taking your word for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-29-2018, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T03:57:25-07:00","id":1212989,"title":"","content":"Hmm, interesting. <b>Crippling Pressure Point Strike</b> can really, <i><b>really</b></i> screw over foes if you don't reset your initiative (or drop by gambit difficulty + 1). Either blind or knock prone or paralyze one of their arms.<br /> <br /> Trouble is it's halfway up Snake Style.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm looking in the other Martial Arts for debilitating effects because those are the only things that are combo-ok (a ha) with White Veil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 04-29-2018, 07:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T07:06:25-07:00","id":1213046,"title":"","content":"The thing is Crippling Pressure Point Strike is specifically a gambit creating Charm, and Birdsong Over Blades calls for successfully landing a Decisive Attack and those two things are not compatible.<br /> <br /> It has been clarified by the Devs that if a Charm calls for a Decisive Attack, that is a regular Decisive Attack, not Gambits, unless specifically stated otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T07:08:51-07:00","id":1213047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1213046#post1213046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is Crippling Pressure Point Strike is specifically a gambit creating Charm, and Birdsong Over Blades calls for successfully landing a Decisive Attack and those two things are not compatible.<br /> <br /> It has been clarified by the Devs that if a Charm calls for a Decisive Attack, that is a regular Decisive Attack, not Gambits, unless specifically stated otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh? I'd read differently previously. Where was this? (Not gainsaying you, just would like to see the quote)<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T07:49:23-07:00","id":1213053,"title":"","content":"Page 50 of the Ask the Devs thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1075221#post1075221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gambits don't benefit from anything that boosts decisive damage\u2014the Initiative roll isn't the same thing as a damage roll. In addition, Charms that let you make decisive attacks part of their activation, like Trance of Unhesitating Speed or Solar Counterattack, mean damaging attacks, not gambits, unless specified otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3559_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3559\" data-vbnamecard=\"3559\">Lanaya</a> for the compilation document at <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1071084-unofficial-dev-ruling-compilation\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ng-compilation</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T08:17:56-07:00","id":1213059,"title":"","content":"White Veil Style is giving me the idea of what is definitely to be my next character when I have the chance.<br /> <br /> I want a Combat Stealth + Disguise Larceny Monster. With everyone he incapacitates he disappears and comes back as another person. Even more terrifying with Killing Shroud Technique. You can come back <i>as the person you just killed, to keep killing their friends.</i> And nobody will be none the wiser! Just too cool. It is not too synergistic with KST, KST is just needed to substitute specific people. But with Mind Shroud Meditation and Flashing Ruse Prana, you can come back as different generic people to spread the murder on. You can a kill a whole crowd, one by one, without anyone realizing. <br /> <br /> Like a terrifying breeze that murders anyone it touches. Imagine walking into a place where this has taken place. Scary shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T08:24:57-07:00","id":1213064,"title":"","content":"Effects like Flexing the Emerald Claw which apply poisons combo with The Dragon Succumbs as well as Birdsong Over Blades. Storm-Calming Embrace combos decently with The Dragon Dies Screaming. Really, all of these form a cluster of &lt;everything that applies or takes advantage of poison, useable alongside bare-handed unarmored martial arts&gt;. <br /> Outside of Martial Arts, Blithe Unruffled Plumage combos with things that improve Guile, eg. Guarded Thoughts Meditation.<br /> The ability to apply poisons, diseases and other on-decisive-hit effects without resetting to base is strong with Snake Style's desire to stay at higher initiative, even without using gambits/essence venom strike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T12:07:15-07:00","id":1213143,"title":"","content":"White Veil + Black Claw<br /> - Thematically, totally not attacking the person who is trying to unjustly murder you &quot;fits.&quot;<br /> - Synergy in that both want Guile 6, Manipulation 5.<br /> - Flexing the Emerald Claw is a low cost, shallow charn that can deliver poison and let you play the feel of WV early.<br /> - White Veil adds Soak, a defense BC doesnt have.<br /> - Attacking someone with both of these styles is a disaster waiting to happen. You can lose up to 6+Intimacy initiative on top of 5 dice unsoakable withering damage.<br /> <br /> White Veil and Silver Voiced Nightingale<br /> There isn't much synergy here, though I like the mystique. You could have SVN handle your withering attacks White Veil supplements the decisive attacks.<br /> <br /> White Veil and Dreaming Pearl Courtesan<br /> DPC allows for shirt ranged attacks, a no WP Decidive finisher, and some evasion/soak benefits. I don't see nuch synergy here, but I could see a character having both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T02:20:57-07:00","id":1214086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1213059#post1213059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Veil Style is giving me the idea of what is definitely to be my next character when I have the chance.<br /> <br /> I want a Combat Stealth + Disguise Larceny Monster. With everyone he incapacitates he disappears and comes back as another person. Even more terrifying with Killing Shroud Technique. You can come back <i>as the person you just killed, to keep killing their friends.</i> And nobody will be none the wiser! Just too cool. It is not too synergistic with KST, KST is just needed to substitute specific people. But with Mind Shroud Meditation and Flashing Ruse Prana, you can come back as different generic people to spread the murder on. You can a kill a whole crowd, one by one, without anyone realizing.<br /> <br /> Like a terrifying breeze that murders anyone it touches. Imagine walking into a place where this has taken place. Scary shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to introduce you to a little game called <i>Prototype</i>... The only reason I'm not playing an Alex Mercer Solar is because I might wanna play an Alex Mercer Lunar or Alex Mercer Exigent.<br /> <br /> Imagine finishing the charm trees for Brawl, Resistance, Athletics, Larceny, Melee (<i>your own body</i>), and having a Thrown Specialty (Vehicles).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 05-02-2018, 05:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T03:39:04-07:00","id":1214094,"title":"","content":"With the synergy, though, I think it's a thematically appropriate mix of MAs, and probably very fun, but there's some problems. You can't disguise your Flexing the Emerald Claw decisives with Bridsong Over Blades, because it needs to deal damage to poison, and Pearlescent Filigree Defense instantly disables White Veil and Black Claw. That's just the low Essence problems I instantly thought of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T04:12:33-07:00","id":1214099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214094#post1214094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the synergy, though, I think it's a thematically appropriate mix of MAs, and probably very fun, but there's some problems. You can't disguise your Flexing the Emerald Claw decisives with Bridsong Over Blades, because it needs to deal damage to poison, and Pearlescent Filigree Defense instantly disables White Veil and Black Claw. That's just the low Essence problems I instantly thought of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do you read that Flexing the Emerald Claw must do damage to work? It doesn't, unlike Snake's Essence Venom Strike, which specifically mentions it does, or Crippling Pressure-Point Attack, which is a Gambit.<br /> <br /> As it stands, Birdsong Over Blades + Flexing the Emerald Claw is a legal combo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T04:16:39-07:00","id":1214100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214086#post1214086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd like to introduce you to a little game called <i>Prototype</i>... The only reason I'm not playing an Alex Mercer Solar is because I might wanna play an Alex Mercer Lunar or Alex Mercer Exigent.<br /> <br /> Imagine finishing the charm trees for Brawl, Resistance, Athletics, Larceny, Melee (<i>your own body</i>), and having a Thrown Specialty (Vehicles).</div> </div> </div> </div>Will check it out! Though probably won't play, had to kind of give up on video games after becoming a father. One must choose his hobbies, and I chose TTRPG, as they're easier to step away from than games, for me. I've tried and used many drugs, and never got addicted. But holy shit, video games, specially MMORPGs, will consume my life and cause me problems before I step away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T04:33:44-07:00","id":1214105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214099#post1214099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where do you read that Flexing the Emerald Claw must do damage to work? It doesn't, unlike Snake's Essence Venom Strike, which specifically mentions it does, or Crippling Pressure-Point Attack, which is a Gambit.<br /> <br /> As it stands, Birdsong Over Blades + Flexing the Emerald Claw is a legal combo.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah my fault, I was going by this post:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page732\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page732\"> Ask the Devs - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page732\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page732 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Dear Exalted fans, as you may be aware from the latest Onyx Path Monday Meeting notes (http://theonyxpath.com/princes-gambit-joy-exalted-plans-monday-meeting-notes/), Robert Vance and I have been honored with the opportunity to take on line editor duties for Exalted Third Edition. As part of that, we want to make ourselves available to the community as a resource to keep you informed as best we can about the line. Obviously there will be some questions we can't answer! But when we're not working on upcoming books, we'll drop in to touch base. We'll be using this thread as our port of call so that we </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And didn't remember that Essence Venom Strike calls out for damage specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T06:10:05-07:00","id":1214121,"title":"","content":"Hmm, could I use this thread to workshop a semi-coherent (aren't they all) beginners build for a Dawn White Veil / Black Claw stylist? Then everyone can point and laugh! (Please don't point and laugh).<br /> <br /> I'm one of the unrepentent concept school of character creation in that I make the concept, then I bolt on cool backstory/traits/etc.<br /> <br /> Core Concepts:<br /> - Manipulation and Guile play a lot into the synergy between the two styles, these two values will have to be maxed.<br /> <br /> - There is some poison synergy in White Veil and Black Claw, Black Claw at low levels and White Veil at High Levels. Also, no Initiative loss from poisoning (but no damage) - early fight debilitation?<br /> <br /> - Core abilities for the combos:<br /> <br /> 1. Martial Arts in White Veil and Black Claw, will have to be maxed, a long with Dexterity.<br /> 2. Socialize to maximize Guile, will also have to be maxed, a long with Manipulation.<br /> <br /> - Secondary abilities:<br /> 1. Stealth - White Veil is very synergistic with high Stealth, and gets one of the most mote efficient stealth booster in the game. Imagine, if you will, 3m for up to around 7 dice?<br /> 2. Black Claw more or less depends on instilling Intimacies, thus Influence forming abilities must be high (presence, really) - Key off Appearance or Manipulation? Not enough points to max Charisma as well.<br /> <br /> -Tertiary:<br /> ??? Can determine later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T08:04:10-07:00","id":1214161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214121#post1214121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, could I use this thread to workshop a semi-coherent (aren't they all) beginners build for a Dawn White Veil / Black Claw stylist? Then everyone can point and laugh! (Please don't point and laugh).<br /> <br /> I'm one of the unrepentent concept school of character creation in that I make the concept, then I bolt on cool backstory/traits/etc.<br /> <br /> Core Concepts:<br /> - Manipulation and Guile play a lot into the synergy between the two styles, these two values will have to be maxed.<br /> <br /> - There is some poison synergy in White Veil and Black Claw, Black Claw at low levels and White Veil at High Levels. Also, no Initiative loss from poisoning (but no damage) - early fight debilitation?<br /> <br /> - Core abilities for the combos:<br /> <br /> 1. Martial Arts in White Veil and Black Claw, will have to be maxed, a long with Dexterity.<br /> 2. Socialize to maximize Guile, will also have to be maxed, a long with Manipulation.<br /> <br /> - Secondary abilities:<br /> 1. Stealth - White Veil is very synergistic with high Stealth, and gets one of the most mote efficient stealth booster in the game. Imagine, if you will, 3m for up to around 7 dice?<br /> 2. Black Claw more or less depends on instilling Intimacies, thus Influence forming abilities must be high (presence, really) - Key off Appearance or Manipulation? Not enough points to max Charisma as well.<br /> <br /> -Tertiary:<br /> ??? Can determine later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you really set on a Dawn? Depending on how you spend motes stealth will start being pretty impossible, the only easy fix for this that I can see is Essence 3 and fairly deep into Stealth, Sun Swallowing Practice, which would not be a big problem, cause Stealth is one the things you want (maybe not that deep into that specific branch though), but again, it is only available to a Dawn at Essence 3.<br /> <br /> Oh! Another way may be through Ebon Shadow Form, which turns your Anima into a shapeless and dark mantle, that while doesn't state outright that it lets you stealth while glowing, that is the subtext I understood, your mileage may vary because of ST interpretation.<br /> <br /> Also consider the value of having Brawl/MA be your Supernal. Most MA Charms are low hanging fruit. I think all cap at Essence 3, and most are E1 or E2. So being a Dawn for that Supernal is not too important if you expect the game to last at least until Essence 3.<br /> <br /> While if you were a Night, your Anima lets you treat Peripheral expenditures as Personal, for 2 motes, which would let you keep stealthing. Plus you can Supernal Socialize or Larceny.<br /> <br /> Now for Synergies:<br /> <br /> Speaking of Ebon Shadow, some early Charms have good synergy, Nothing But Shadows is just plain good, penalizing attempts to keep you out of stealth, and gives you a way out if someone sees trhough your shenenigans and hits you. Seven Points of Weakness Strike is a great boost to a stealthed withering attack, poison them, then crash them and watch them die. If you're willing to go 2 deeper, Shadow-Stepping Motion, is also very decent and thematic.<br /> <br /> Socialize has the perfect Guarded Thoughts Meditation, 4m committed for Indefinite +3 Guile at Essence 2, this is a must have. For Intimacy creating goodness, Energic Influence Technique is very good along with the very thematic Indecent Proposal Method, though Socialize instills would need Presence's Poised Lion Attitude to work nicely. I would also take a Socialize Specialty (In Disguise) and have Guile 6 while disguised, baseline.<br /> <br /> In Presence there are many options, to keep to theme I would take the seduction branch all the way to Rose-Lipped Seduction Style, which includes an Appearance cap breaker, Majestic Radiant Presence to make it even harder to target you, Poised Lion Attitude for no penalty flurries and up to Fulminating Word and Excellent friend approach, to make your Black Claw Presence based instills that much harder to resist, and to make use of those Intimacies to boss people around.<br /> <br /> Next we have Performance, which I would take up to Thousand Courtesan Ways, for the add on seduction with instills and another Appearance cap breaker, and Master Thespian Style, which is a scene long +1 Guile for one mote, if you stay in character, which expressly works with Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise. So choose a character to play while you murder people.<br /> <br /> Larceny has the disguise branch I would take for theme and awesomeness, depending how deep you\u00b4re willing to go, it will have some good synergies with Stealth too. And Fate-Shifting Solar Arete for general amazingness.<br /> <br /> Stealth has the whole combat stealth branch, which is pretty bread and butter, but I can comment if you have doubts about it.<br /> <br /> So lets look at this guy's Guile:<br /> <br /> Maxxed Base: Guile 5 (0m)<br /> <br /> Specialty - In Disguise + Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise: +1 Guile (6m)<br /> <br /> Guarded Thoughts Meditation: +3 Guile (4m)<br /> <br /> Master Thespian Style: +1 Guile (1m)<br /> <br /> White Veil Form: +1 Guile (7m)<br /> <br /> Total Guile: 11 Total Commitment: 18m<br /> <br /> You can commit more motes to have up to Appearance 7, to reduce cost of Social Influence Charms, or to force people to have to pay Willpower to attack, if they can locate you and see through your disguise first, that is. And even if they see through all this deception, they might not be able to help themselves and just fall in love with you. Ain't that a bitch?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ah Also forgot Dodge's Rumor of Form, as another in combat stealth attempt option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 05-02-2018, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T08:15:01-07:00","id":1214166,"title":"","content":"Ebon Shadow Form disguises your anima, not hides it.<br /> <br /> It hides your distinctive colors and iconography. But it is still just as big and bright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T08:20:39-07:00","id":1214169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214161#post1214161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you really set on a Dawn? Depending on how you spend motes stealth will start being pretty impossible, the only easy fix for this that I can see is Essence 3 and fairly deep into Stealth, Sun Swallowing Practice, which would not be a big problem, cause Stealth is one the things you want (maybe not that deep into that specific branch though), but again, it is only available to a Dawn at Essence 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, Stealth is more utility/first strike for a starting Martial Artists. Personally I just wanted the combination of Doe Eyes Defence / Torn Lotus Defence to almost Crash people who attack me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh! Another way may be through Ebon Shadow Form, which turns your Anima into a shapeless and dark mantle, that while doesn't state outright that it lets you stealth while glowing, that is the subtext I understood, your mileage may vary because of ST interpretation.<br /> <br /> Also consider the value of having Brawl/MA be your Supernal. Most MA Charms are low hanging fruit. I think all cap at Essence 3, and most are E1 or E2. So being a Dawn for that Supernal is not too important if you expect the game to last at least until Essence 3. </div> </div> </div>Call me shallow, but I tend to like to go for the easy power combos at Ess 1, then work my way up. It takes quite a while to get to Ess 3, even with regular games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While if you were a Night, your Anima lets you treat Peripheral expenditures as Personal, for 2 motes, which would let you keep stealthing. Plus you can Supernal Socialize or Larceny. </div> </div> </div>Depends if you want to focus on the Stealthing or the Fighting. For me, I kind of want to be Exalted Female Zorro, rather than a Kunoichi (though I suppose she is that as well).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now for Synergies:<br /> <br /> Speaking of Ebon Shadow, some early Charms have good synergy, Nothing But Shadows is just plain good, penalizing attempts to keep you out of stealth, and gives you a way out if someone sees trhough your shenenigans and hits you. Seven Points of Weakness Strike is a great boost to a stealthed withering attack, poison them, then crash them and watch them die. If you're willing to go 2 deeper, Shadow-Stepping Motion, is also very decent and thematic. </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I'll go re-read Ebon Shadow again, to be honest, I was going to splash Snake for the early boosters. Once again, Stealth or Fighting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Socialize has the perfect Guarded Thoughts Meditation, 4m committed for Indefinite +3 Guile at Essence 2, this is a must have. For Intimacy creating goodness, Energic Influence Technique is very good along with the very thematic Indecent Proposal Method, though Socialize instills would need Presence's Poised Lion Attitude to work nicely. I would also take a Socialize Specialty (In Disguise) and have Guile 6 while disguised, baseline. </div> </div> </div>Ohh yeah, Socialize gets some purchases. Definitely Shadow over Day to start off with, but at Ess 2, definitely (to win even harder). The disguise is a good idea for later synergies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Presence there are many options, to keep to theme I would take the seduction branch all the way to Rose-Lipped Seduction Style, which includes an Appearance cap breaker, Majestic Radiant Presence to make it even harder to target you, Poised Lion Attitude for no penalty flurries and up to Fulminating Word and Excellent friend approach, to make your Black Claw Presence based instills that much harder to resist, and to make use of those Intimacies to boss people around. </div> </div> </div>Mercy! I only have so many charms. Good news is, Charms are cheap to buy in game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Next we have Performance, which I would take up to Thousand Courtesan Ways, for the add on seduction with instills and another Appearance cap breaker, and Master Thespian Style, which is a scene long +1 Guile for one mote, if you stay in character, which expressly works with Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise. So choose a character to play while you murder people. </div> </div> </div>Definitely good value buys.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Larceny has the disguise branch I would take for theme and awesomeness, depending how deep you\u00b4re willing to go, it will have some good synergies with Stealth too. And Fate-Shifting Solar Arete for general amazingness.<br /> <br /> Stealth has the whole combat stealth branch, which is pretty bread and butter, but I can comment if you have doubts about it. </div> </div> </div>Heh, You've convinced me to possibly splash Larceny.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So lets look at this guy's Guile:<br /> <br /> Maxxed Base: Guile 5 (0m)<br /> <br /> Specialty - In Disguise + Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise: +1 Guile (6m)<br /> <br /> Guarded Thoughts Meditation: +3 Guile (4m)<br /> <br /> Master Thespian Style: +1 Guile (1m)<br /> <br /> White Veil Form: +1 Guile (7m)<br /> <br /> Total Guile: 11 Total Commitment: 18m<br /> <br /> You can commit more motes to have up to Appearance 7, to reduce cost of Social Influence Charms, or to force people to have to pay Willpower to attack, if they can locate you and see through your disguise first, that is. And even if they see through all this deception, they might not be able to help themselves and just fall in love with you. Ain't that a bitch?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ah Also forgot Dodge's Rumor of Form, as another in combat stealth attempt option. </div> </div> </div>Thats alot of commitment, once again I'll be aiming a bit for low hanging stuff to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 05-02-2018, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T08:58:39-07:00","id":1214182,"title":"","content":"Alright so here's what I got. (First Draft to be revised)<br /> <br /> <i><b>Mistress Dusk</b></i> - Renowned Tea Ceremony Master by day, Virtuous Assassin by night!<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b><br /> <br /> Physical (Secondary)<br /> <br /> Strength OOO<br /> Dexterity OOOOO<br /> Stamina O<br /> <br /> Social (Primary)<br /> <br /> Charisma O<br /> Manipulation OOOOO<br /> Appearance OOOOO<br /> <br /> Mental (Tertiary)<br /> <br /> Perception OO<br /> Intelligence OOO<br /> Wits OO<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities:<br /> <br /> C</b> Brawl O<br /> <b>C</b> Martial Arts (White Veil) OOOOO<br /> <b>C</b> Martial Arts (Black Claw) OOOOO (Razor Sharp Nails)<br /> <b>C</b> Dodge OOOOO (Hair's Breadth Evasions)<br /> <b>C</b> Resistance OO<br /> <b>F</b> Larceny OOOOO<br /> <b>F</b> Presence OOOOO (Graceful Appeal)<br /> <b>F</b> Socialize OOOOO (Keeping others guessing)<br /> <b>F</b> Stealth OOOOO<br /> <b>F</b> Performance OOO<br /> Linguistics O<br /> <br /> <b>Merits: </b><br /> <br /> Martial Arts OOOO<br /> Artifact (Silken Robes) OOOO<br /> Resources OO<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Charms: </b><br /> <br /> <u>Black Claw </u><br /> Open Palm Caress<br /> Torn Lotus Defense<br /> Flexing the Emerald Claw<br /> Black Claw Form<br /> Doe Eyes Defense<br /> <br /> <u>White Veil</u><br /> Birdsong Over Blades<br /> Alehouse Memory Stance<br /> <br /> <u>Dodge</u><br /> Reed in the Wind<br /> Drifting Leaf Elusion<br /> Shadow over Water<br /> Searing Quicksilver Flight<br /> <br /> <u>Presence</u><br /> Harmonious Presence Meditation<br /> Poised Lion Attitude<br /> <br /> <u>Socialize</u><br /> Shadow over Day<br /> <br /> <u>Resistance</u><br /> Ox Body Technique<br /> <br /> Phew! I will probably have to change things around. No time before bed, but I'll probably give my reasoning for things tomorrow.<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 05-02-2018, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T09:26:00-07:00","id":1214193,"title":"","content":"Query: Does Guile Raised by Charms count for the calculation of Doe Eyes Defense et al? Or is it base Guile only?<br /> <br /> I also take it you can't Stunt Guile while activating charms, yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T10:03:14-07:00","id":1214201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214193#post1214193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Query: Does Guile Raised by Charms count for the calculation of Doe Eyes Defense et al? Or is it base Guile only?<br /> <br /> I also take it you can't Stunt Guile while activating charms, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Base only.<br /> <br /> Guile is a static value, and I can't remember any restrictions on stunting it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T10:10:14-07:00","id":1214204,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8959_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8959\" data-vbnamecard=\"8959\">prototype00</a> <br /> \u200b<br /> You got your Caste Abilities wrong, if you Caste/Favor Brawl, you automatically Caste/Favor all Martial Arts. You only need to spend one option on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T11:41:05-07:00","id":1214235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214166#post1214166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ebon Shadow Form disguises your anima, not hides it.<br /> <br /> It hides your distinctive colors and iconography. But it is still just as big and bright.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, like I said, it is open to interpretation. Might be a good one for the Ask the Devs thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T12:47:26-07:00","id":1214270,"title":"","content":"Yah, no stealth while flaring in Ebon Shadow Form, so scratch that option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T16:17:19-07:00","id":1214351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214204#post1214204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8959_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8959\" data-vbnamecard=\"8959\">prototype00</a><br /> \u200b<br /> You got your Caste Abilities wrong, if you Caste/Favor Brawl, you automatically Caste/Favor all Martial Arts. You only need to spend one option on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only spent one Caste pick on it. Why did you think I didn't? I just don't have enough points to put in my other caste abilities, Awareness and Thrown.<br /> <br /> In the cold light of the morning though, I'm probably going to re-arrange abilities a tad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 05-02-2018, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T16:37:22-07:00","id":1214356,"title":"","content":"THE MANTIS MATING DANCE<br /> Open Palm Caress<br /> Torn Lotus Defense<br /> Flexing the Emerald Claw<br /> Black Claw Form<br /> Storm Calming Embrace<br /> Iron Arm Block<br /> Crushing Claw Technique<br /> Mantis Form<br /> Joint-Locking Technique<br /> Birdsong Over Blades<br /> (Optional) Doe Eyes Defense<br /> (Optional) Grasping Claw Method<br /> (Optional) Grasping Claw Defense<br /> Total = 10 to 13 Charms<br /> <br /> Use Birdsong Over Blades with Flexing the Emerald Claw to poison the target, retain your initiative for the followup grapple, and give them -5 to resist the poison. Then establish a Grapple with Storm Calming Embrace. If you open with Open Palm Caress you can make this an ambush instead of spending a ton of motes to hit. If you then hit with the Grapple and they are not immune to poison/grapple, then they are probably dead.<br /> <br /> Total Cost: <br /> Hit with two decisives<br /> DECISIVE 1: Flexing the Emerald Claw + Birdsong Over Blades + Open Palm Caress Ambush = 9m, 1wp<br /> GRAPPLE GAMBIT: Storm-Calling Embrace + Crushing Claw Technique + Excellencies =5m, 1wp + Excellencies (max +8 on the attack roll, +5 on the Control Roll)<br /> <br /> EVERY TURN AFTER: 5m per turn for Joint-Locking <br /> <br /> This combo is fairly reliable as well. Its difficult to avoid ambushes, and the Grapple attack roll is going to average AROUND 14.3 Successes if you go all in and have maximun dex/ma. <br /> <br /> To improve on this combo, I would add the rest of White Veil. The Dragon Dies Screaming is a *far* better Poison... and, yanno, they stack and you can deliver both on the same attack. Thats also a lot more charms, so ymmv.<br /> <br /> Maxed, these three styles combine well offensively. Mantis' capstone works amidst Storm-Calling Embrace and the resulting -(A Lot) Onslaught can, via Tickling the Dragon's Throat, be persisted basically for the rest of the fight, assuming they somehow survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 05-02-2018, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T16:56:40-07:00","id":1214362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214201#post1214201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Base only.<br /> <br /> Guile is a static value, and I can't remember any restrictions on stunting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So really, the most you can penalize someone with DED is 6 dice, ever. (7 if they allow stunting the defence)<br /> <br /> I mean, still good, but great...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T17:25:27-07:00","id":1214368,"title":"","content":"You know whats really slow? Poisoning and grappling. You know whats efficient? 20 HLs of damage in addition to actually rolling damage. Lets make that happen.<br /> <br /> THE JUMPSCARE<br /> Birdsong Over Blades<br /> Owl Clutches the Night<br /> Alehouse Memory Stance<br /> White Veil Form<br /> Blithe Unruffled Plumage<br /> Blinded By Laughter<br /> Nothing But Shadows<br /> Seven Points of Weakness Strike<br /> Ebon Shadow Form<br /> Shadow Stepping Motion<br /> Throat-Slitting Shadow Atemi<br /> Monkey Leap Technique<br /> Increasing Strength Exorcise<br /> Thunderbolt Attack Prana<br /> Total = 14 Charms<br /> <br /> Its simple, you're enjoying a party over in a corner. Then, all of a sudden, you are somewhere within short range and someone is very dead.<br /> <br /> Combining Blinded by Laughter and Throat-Slitting Shadow Atemi and Thunderbolt Attack Prana means that you make an Ambush (vs 0 Defense) where up to 11 Successes above defense are added to the damage roll. Every successes above defense converts a die of raw damage into an automatic success. Then, after all of that plus your actual initiative, you double your damage.<br /> <br /> That said, this may be too many charms to be worth rushing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T17:54:45-07:00","id":1214374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214362#post1214362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So really, the most you can penalize someone with DED is 6 dice, ever. (7 if they allow stunting the defence)<br /> <br /> I mean, still good, but great...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind its acting as a penalty to their attack while you are still capable of boosting your defense fully with an excellency or other defensive charms. At a cost of 4m and 1i i would say a -6 penalty is amazing especially if you have the mastery effect of recouping initiative. Consider it would take them 6m to offset the -6 which would be part of their cap for boosting.<br /> <br /> Edit: another way of looking at it is its sort of the equivalent of +3dv non charm bonus if you have 6 guile","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5167,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","user":"Klaek","date":". 05-02-2018, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T23:48:40-07:00","id":1214442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Klaek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214374#post1214374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Keep in mind its acting as a penalty to their attack while you are still capable of boosting your defense fully with an excellency or other defensive charms. At a cost of 4m and 1i i would say a -6 penalty is amazing especially if you have the mastery effect of recouping initiative. Consider it would take them 6m to offset the -6 which would be part of their cap for boosting.<br /> <br /> Edit: another way of looking at it is its sort of the equivalent of +3dv non charm bonus if you have 6 guile</div> </div> </div> </div>True, true. A couple of further thoughts:<br /> <br /> - white veils gnarly later poisons make Storm Calmig Embrace and a decent Strength worth it (alas, my Stamina. I will build you up, anon)<br /> <br /> - Form charm wise, I\u2019d stick to Black Claw as it\u2019s more combat focused.<br /> <br /> - but Blithe Unruffled Plumage will be definitely worth it to take. So you\u2019ll end up with the Form Charms of both.<br /> <br /> - what\u2019s a good opening? Poison and then Storm Valming Embrace or Stealth into Heart Ripping Claw?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T00:33:42-07:00","id":1214456,"title":"","content":"Black Claw really likes instilling people. White Veil Form gives free Socialize flurries. If you're Solar then you can throw in Poised Lion Attitude for <i>another</i> free (from flurry penalties) social action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T02:14:08-07:00","id":1214485,"title":"","content":"We\u2019ll see, that\u2019s the thing, you\u2019ll probably do most of your flurrying with Poised Lion Attitude (White Veil Form is harder than Black Claw to activate reflexively), so the free socialize flurry seems kind of... extra? Superfluous?<br /> <br /> The only thing that stacks is Thousand Courtesan Ways which instills an additional Positive Intimacy (lust) at the same time, and expressly isn\u2019t a flurry (which fair enough strips Willpower from a foe right quick when combined together)<br /> <br /> Other than that Black Claw form is generally better in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 05-03-2018, 05:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T02:43:24-07:00","id":1214498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214368#post1214368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know whats really slow? Poisoning and grappling. You know whats efficient? 20 HLs of damage in addition to actually rolling damage. Lets make that happen.<br /> <br /> THE JUMPSCARE<br /> Birdsong Over Blades<br /> Owl Clutches the Night<br /> Alehouse Memory Stance<br /> White Veil Form<br /> Blithe Unruffled Plumage<br /> Blinded By Laughter<br /> Nothing But Shadows<br /> Seven Points of Weakness Strike<br /> Ebon Shadow Form<br /> Shadow Stepping Motion<br /> Throat-Slitting Shadow Atemi<br /> Monkey Leap Technique<br /> Increasing Strength Exorcise<br /> Thunderbolt Attack Prana<br /> Total = 14 Charms<br /> <br /> Its simple, you're enjoying a party over in a corner. Then, all of a sudden, you are somewhere within short range and someone is very dead.<br /> <br /> Combining Blinded by Laughter and Throat-Slitting Shadow Atemi and Thunderbolt Attack Prana means that you make an Ambush (vs 0 Defense) where up to 11 Successes above defense are added to the damage roll. Every successes above defense converts a die of raw damage into an automatic success. Then, after all of that plus your actual initiative, you double your damage.<br /> <br /> That said, this may be too many charms to be worth rushing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, usually it's the ninja that suddenly vanishes in a puff of smoke, not their victims.<br /> <br /> That said, a starting Dawn with these charms and Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise for his fifteenth would be hilarious to play. Call him Understudy, because he steps into the role of anyone who might mysteriously disappear in the middle of the night, or the middle of the day, or the middle of a sentence. Much classier than &quot;the Vanisher&quot;, imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T09:23:28-07:00","id":1214640,"title":"","content":"Alright, take two!<br /> <br /> <i><b>Mistress Dusk</b></i> - Renowned Tea Ceremony Master by day, Virtuous Assassin by night!<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b><br /> <br /> Physical (Secondary)<br /> <br /> Strength OOO<br /> Dexterity OOOOO<br /> Stamina O<br /> <br /> Social (Primary)<br /> <br /> Charisma O<br /> Manipulation OOOOO<br /> Appearance OOOOO<br /> <br /> Mental (Tertiary)<br /> <br /> Perception OO<br /> Intelligence OO<br /> Wits OOO<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities:<br /> <br /> C</b> Brawl O<br /> <b>C</b> Martial Arts (White Veil) OOOOO<br /> <b>C</b> Martial Arts (Black Claw) OOOOO (Razor Sharp Nails)<br /> <b>C</b> Dodge OOOOO (Hair's Breadth Evasions)<br /> <b>C</b> Resistance<br /> <b>C</b> Awareness<br /> <b>C </b>Thrown<br /> <b>F</b> Presence OOOOO (Graceful Appeal)<br /> <b>F</b> Socialize OOOOO (Keeping others guessing)<br /> <b>F</b> Stealth OOOOO<br /> <b>F</b> Performance OOO<br /> <b>F </b>Occult OOO<br /> Linguistics O<br /> <br /> <b>Merits: </b><br /> <br /> Martial Arts OOOO<br /> Artifact (Silken Robes) OOOO<br /> Resources O<br /> Artifact (Belt of Shadow Walking) OOO<br /> <br /> <b>Charms: </b><br /> <br /> <u>Black Claw </u><br /> Open Palm Caress<br /> Torn Lotus Defense<br /> Flexing the Emerald Claw<br /> Black Claw Form<br /> Doe Eyes Defense<br /> <br /> <u>White Veil</u><br /> Birdsong Over Blades<br /> Alehouse Memory Stance<br /> <br /> <u>Performance</u><br /> Masterful Performance Exercise<br /> Thousand Courtesan Ways<br /> <br /> <u>Dodge</u><br /> Reed in the Wind<br /> Drifting Leaf Elusion<br /> Shadow over Water<br /> Searing Quicksilver Flight<br /> <br /> <u>Presence</u><br /> Harmonious Presence Meditation<br /> Poised Lion Attitude<br /> <br /> There we go, that's a bit more well rounded. I've taken some value buys of abilities that will become useful in very short order, but the hour grows late and I will expound tomorrow.<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T12:20:18-07:00","id":1214724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214362#post1214362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So really, the most you can penalize someone with DED is 6 dice, ever. (7 if they allow stunting the defence)<br /> <br /> I mean, still good, but great...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually DED is Guile + Intimacy (if positive)<br /> <br /> So;<br /> <br /> Base 6<br /> <br /> Stunts<br /> <br /> Stunt 1 = +1<br /> Stunt 2 = +2<br /> Stunt 3 = +3<br /> <br /> Positive Intimacy<br /> <br /> Minor = +2<br /> Major = +3<br /> Defining = +4<br /> <br /> So anywhere from 6 to 13. But basically hovering on 9, with a stunt 1 and a Minor Positive Intimacy, which is very doable for a BC practitioner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T16:35:03-07:00","id":1214826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214724#post1214724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually DED is Guile + Intimacy (if positive)<br /> <br /> So;<br /> <br /> Base 6<br /> <br /> Stunts<br /> <br /> Stunt 1 = +1<br /> Stunt 2 = +2<br /> Stunt 3 = +3<br /> <br /> Positive Intimacy<br /> <br /> Minor = +2<br /> Major = +3<br /> Defining = +4<br /> <br /> So anywhere from 6 to 13. But basically hovering on 9, with a stunt 1 and a Minor Positive Intimacy, which is very doable for a BC practitioner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, see, I don't know if you get to stunt your guile mid-charm activation to raise it's value, and the Devs haven't answered yet. But yes, from 6 to 13, probably averaging around 9 dice in penalty.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ah! You can\u2019t stunt your Guile for this as per Vance\u2019s reply. So somewhere around a -8 penalty, unless they have been spending Willpower to resist your Instills. <br /> <br /> Still, not bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 05-03-2018, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T18:57:04-07:00","id":1214873,"title":"","content":"So to review my mad choices:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214640#post1214640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, take two!<br /> <br /> <i><b>Mistress Dusk</b></i> - Renowned Tea Ceremony Master by day, Virtuous Assassin by night!</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured that the high Socialize angle would be good for someone who gets her info from performing tea ceremonies for the rich and corrupt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Attributes:</b><br /> <br /> Physical (Secondary)<br /> <br /> Strength OOO<br /> Dexterity OOOOO<br /> Stamina O<br /> <br /> Social (Primary)<br /> <br /> Charisma O<br /> Manipulation OOOOO<br /> Appearance OOOOO<br /> <br /> Mental (Tertiary)<br /> <br /> Perception OO<br /> Intelligence OO<br /> Wits OOO </div> </div> </div>The attributes could be a bit less Min-Maxxed... I find having a 1 in a couple of Attributes makes for an interesting backstory, however.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Abilities:<br /> <br /> C</b> Brawl O<br /> <b>C</b> Martial Arts (White Veil) OOOOO<br /> <b>C</b> Martial Arts (Black Claw) OOOOO (Razor Sharp Nails)<br /> <b>C</b> Dodge OOOOO (Hair's Breadth Evasions)<br /> <b>C</b> Resistance<br /> <b>C</b> Awareness<br /> <b>C </b>Thrown<br /> <b>F</b> Presence OOOOO (Graceful Appeal)<br /> <b>F</b> Socialize OOOOO (Keeping others guessing)<br /> <b>F</b> Stealth OOOOO<br /> <b>F</b> Performance OOO<br /> <b>F </b>Occult OOO<br /> Linguistics O </div> </div> </div>Did you know that dots 4 and 5 in abilities is the best use of your BP during character creation? It\u2019s true!<br /> <br /> So a brief rundown:<br /> <br /> Combat:<br /> <br /> Martial Arts (White Veil/Black Claw)- it\u2019s efficient to buy a<br /> MA up to 5 at character creation if you are going to be getting high level Charms for it.<br /> Dodge - Dodge is the main defence for all of these styles<br /> <br /> Sideboard: Snake Style 3 dots. Replace Occult with this. Snake Styles first two Charms are great and synergistic for this character but not worth Deep investment.<br /> <br /> Social:<br /> <br /> Socialize - You need to max this for Guile.<br /> Presence - You might as well max this to instill with Black Claw<br /> Performance - A value purchase of thousand Courtesan Ways boosts both your Appearance Instills and your Instill attempts count for double. If you need to strip willpower quickly in Social combat, this is the charm for you.<br /> <br /> Others:<br /> <br /> Occult- value purchase for Sorcery easy access, as well as the charms that let you strike Immaterial Foes. With the Belt of Shadow Walking it lets you strike Material foes while Immaterial, which is as good as perfect Defense against certain foes.<br /> <br /> Stealth- A lot of effects from White Ceil benefit Stealth, so you might as well be world renowned in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Merits: </b><br /> <br /> Martial Arts OOOO<br /> Artifact (Silken Robes) OOOO<br /> Resources O<br /> Artifact (Belt of Shadow Walking) OOO </div> </div> </div>Martial Arts and the Silken Armor are non negotiable. Since White Veil gets you one of the most mote efficient Stealth Enhancers, Belt of Shadow Walking gets you 19 Dice for Stealt Checks for a 4m expenditure. Not necessary but nice, as is Resources.<br /> <br /> Charms next post!<br /> <br /> Edit: I just realized who she reminds me of! ZatoIchi! Except not blind. Maybe she could be deaf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 05-03-2018, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T20:54:40-07:00","id":1214898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214485#post1214485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We\u2019ll see, that\u2019s the thing, you\u2019ll probably do most of your flurrying with Poised Lion Attitude (White Veil Form is harder than Black Claw to activate reflexively), so the free socialize flurry seems kind of... extra? Superfluous?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can't figure out how to take advantage of a second free instill action per turn then maybe Black Claw isn't the right style for you. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T21:01:35-07:00","id":1214899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214898#post1214898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you can't figure out how to take advantage of a second free instill action per turn then maybe Black Claw isn't the right style for you. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>It follows the rules of Flurry, which stated only 2 combat actions. You get the same number of actions at no penalty whether you use this or Poised Lion Attitude.<br /> <br /> Edit: I am of course 100% open to being wrong. 3 separate Instill attempts per turn would be sweet!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 05-04-2018, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T21:48:28-07:00","id":1214911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214899#post1214899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It follows the rules of Flurry, which stated only 2 combat actions. You get the same number of actions at no penalty whether you use this or Poised Lion Attitude.<br /> <br /> Edit: I am of course 100% open to being wrong. 3 separate Instill attempts per turn would be sweet!</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case then take that opening, because Poised Lion Attitude does not count as a flurry:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Solar\u2019s presence is such that she affects unnatural<br /> ease, even on the battlefield. This Charm allows the Exalt<br /> to engage in Presence or Socialize-based social influence<br /> on her turn during combat <b>without the use of a flurry</b>.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T21:51:13-07:00","id":1214913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214911#post1214911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In this case then take that opening, because Poised Lion Attitude does not count as a flurry:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Solar\u2019s presence is such that she affects unnatural<br /> ease, even on the battlefield. This Charm allows the Exalt<br /> to engage in Presence or Socialize-based social influence<br /> on her turn during combat <b>without the use of a flurry</b>.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, very nice, that was my mistake then. And it would be 4 Instills as Thousand Courtesan ways triggers twice!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T22:49:05-07:00","id":1214924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214913#post1214913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooh, very nice, that was my mistake then. And it would be 4 Instills as Thousand Courtesan ways triggers twice!</div> </div> </div> </div>And don't forget that with Energic Influence Technique every instill done to intensify an existing intimacy also generates a new related minor intimacy.<br /> <br /> So Torn Lotus Defense + Thousand Courtesan Way to create Minor Positive Tie (Respect, Admiration or Love) + Minor Positive Tie (Lust), Then White Veil Form penalty free Socialize instill flurry + Energic Influence Technique + TCW to intensify the Minor Positive Tie based on the Minor Lust Tie to Major, and get a new Minor Positive Tie, and with TCW's instill intensify the Minor Lust Tie to Major based on the new Minor Positive Tie and then with Poised Lion Attitude +EIT+TCW intensify the Major Positive Tie to Defining based on the Major Lust Tie, get a new Minor positive tie because of EIT and intensify the Major Lust Tie to defining too. And that is not even paying for the TCW instill to have EIT as well, because then that would be another 2 Minor Positive Ties.<br /> <br /> So:<br /> <br /> <br /> TLD + TCW (Since it is Presence based no EIT, and not intensifying, but creating)<br /> <br /> +Minor Tie (Admiration Black Claw Stylist)<br /> +Minor Tie (Lust BCS)<br /> <br /> WVF + EIT + TCW<br /> <br /> Minor Tie (Admiration BCS) &gt; Major, based on Minor Tie (Lust BCS)<br /> +Minor Principle (Talk Things Out)<br /> Minor Tie (Lust BCS) &gt; Major based on, Minor Principle (Talk Things Out)<br /> +Minor Tie (Please BCS)<br /> <br /> PLA + EIT + TCW<br /> <br /> Major Tie (Admiration BCS) &gt; Defining, based on Major Tie (Lust BCS)<br /> +Minor Tie (Protect BCS)<br /> Minor Tie (Please BCS) &gt; Major, based on Minor Tie (Protect BCS)<br /> +Minor Tie (Devotion to BCS)<br /> <br /> End:<br /> <br /> Defining Tie (Admiration BCS)<br /> Major Tie (Lust BCS)<br /> Major Tie (Please BCS)<br /> Minor Tie (Protect BCS)<br /> Minor Tie (Devotion to BCS)<br /> Minor Principle (Talk Things Out)<br /> <br /> \u200bYou can even come out with other intensity distributions, depend how you go about keying the instills.<br /> <br /> All in one counter attack + one round of instills, and you still have a penalty free action to take on this round!<br /> <br /> Of course you gotta roleplay the hell out of this interaction, but it is mechanically possible. I think. LOL.<br /> <br /> May be that it is a little wrong, cause I'm lazy right now, but you get the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T23:00:33-07:00","id":1214926,"title":"","content":"Other than you won\u2019t know the intimacy instilled by a Torn Lotus Defense (Attackers choice) seems very legit. (Though really you only need one positive intimacy to key off mos of Black Claws stuff)<br /> <br /> Though yes, if they are trying to remain clean of your influence, you have successfully tanked their Willpower.<br /> <br /> White Veil/Black Claw really is just Black Claw with a more synergistic pairing than Dreaming Pearl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 05-04-2018, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T00:25:38-07:00","id":1214956,"title":"","content":"Great googly moogly! I just realized that for a mere 4m the Stealth roll of this character is 21(!!!). <br /> <br /> Gotta fit in Blinding Battle Feint somehow...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T02:07:53-07:00","id":1214972,"title":"","content":"Had a great deal of fun with a Black Claw MA dancer. Start your dancing with Respect-Commanding Attitude before attacking and with Black Claw you become basically unhittable. Sure, you have to flurry a dance action every round, but you use it for instilling and compelling of course. <br /> <br /> Between Respect Commanding Attitude, Torn Lotus Defense, Thousand Courtesan Ways, Doe-eyed Defense and Poised Lion Attitude you are set. Your opponents will burn through their willpower at a ridiculous rate and before long they are your loyal and loving minions. Mix in Charms like Wise-Eyed Courtier and Energic Influence Technique to truly disgust your ST. I would look there before going deep in stealth, which imho, is not what Black Claw does best. <br /> <br /> In fact, you should almost never have to resort to damaging decisives and killing opponents. Why would you when you can turn opponents into 'ally' or 'contact' dots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T08:55:33-07:00","id":1215085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1212985#post1212985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So aside from having Mastery*, which Sidereals can also access, what is it that Solars, Abyssals, and Green Sun Princes have in common? Not sorcery (as Abyssals don't have access to the Adamant Circle), not Evocations (as Abyssals are only Resonant with soulsteel), and not Charm design (with Abyssals and Green Sun Princes branching off into Deathlord/shintai directions respectively). It sure isn't in how they're Chosen. Sure, you could say they're all monstrously powerful, but the same is true of Exalted in general.<br /> <br /> Simply put, &quot;Solaroid&quot; is not a good term because the thing it's trying to convey - that you can just lump them all together under the same umbrella - is not a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even in 3e, Solars are PRETTY CLEARLY intended to have, in general, the strongest charm effects, with Abyssals and Infernals [both of which draw on a stolen Solar exaltation, still in 3e] being comparably 'superior'. It's no longer the &quot;Solar is captain america next to Lunar who is an ordinary dude with four broken limbs and DB who is literally in a frickin' iron lung&quot; of 2e but to imply that the Solar 'standing above' in most raw charm power is nonexistent is disingenuous. Mastery and Resonance primarily exist to grant Solars more reason to use MA and artifacts [with the flavor benefit of Sidereals being as good as Solars at MA and non-Exalts being able to draw as much from their magical material as Solars, generally speaking, being secondary benefits creating incentives]; this incentive wouldn't be necessary if MA and Evocations were without those keywords comparable to Solar power [but if they were, then there would need to be disincentives to prevent MA/Evoc being OTB for everyone not-Solar].","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T09:10:16-07:00","id":1215092,"title":"","content":"I don't think the position was that Sidereals would as good at MA as Solars. They would have to do something to access Mastery, it wasn't available all the time, from what I remember was said by the Devs at the time.<br /> <br /> Where they get an advantage is in Sidereal MAs.<br /> <br /> But things change, Sidereals are bit far away, who knows how it end up turning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T09:18:12-07:00","id":1215096,"title":"","content":"More on White Veil Form + Poised Lion Attitude, if brute force double-Instilling isn't your style or ever isn't working out you can use the Form to Read Intentions instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T09:29:52-07:00","id":1215103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1215096#post1215096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More on White Veil Form + Poised Lion Attitude, if brute force double-Instilling isn't your style or ever isn't working out you can use the Form to Read Intentions instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and, Motive-Discerning Technique, Quicksilver Falcon Eyes and Umbral Eyes Focus (I think those are the Charm names) will let you get a very good grasp on what is going on so you can use those instills to better effect.. There are a few others, but these are shallow in the tree and very good workhorses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T12:37:07-07:00","id":1215203,"title":"","content":"The question is, can White Veil form replace SVN as the go-to source of &quot;free&quot; social flurry?<br /> <br /> That is, can you use Socialize to Instill outside of a court context? You *can read intention + Thousand Courtesan Ways to do it, but its competing with SVN's double instill in any context, with an easy love of music / love me dynamic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T14:47:02-07:00","id":1215239,"title":"","content":"TFW: Your thread blows up in a good way when your gone. Also I love people\u2019s build outs. Seeing WV mix and matched is cool. Go ahead and print your character ideas here. The more nuanced and detailed the better. Those have been some great posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T14:59:42-07:00","id":1215244,"title":"","content":"Edit: Nevermind, I cant read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T16:28:19-07:00","id":1215266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1215203#post1215203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is, can you use Socialize to Instill outside of a court context?</div> </div> </div> </div>You see, that is a very good question. In the groups I play, Presence and Socialize are kinda like Charisma and Manipulation, different but sometimes confusingly similar.<br /> <br /> Presence is in your face, magnetic, attention hogging, bigger than life, confidence.<br /> <br /> Socialize is studied, subtle, polite, measured, precise, charming.<br /> <br /> We always played like you could choose which ability you wanted to use for the instills, but the ability descriptor seems a bit hazy in that it is not clear if it can only be used to instill in formal situations, and the only combat use is to read intentions or not. This is a good one for Ask the Devs. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T17:36:07-07:00","id":1215285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1215266#post1215266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a good one for Ask the Devs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely, which is probably why it got <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1080152#post1080152\">asked and answered</a> a year ago. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T17:46:08-07:00","id":1215286,"title":"","content":"White Veil is meant to be practiced in a structured social mileu. I think its meant to let you murderface someone while *also* enjoying a party and sipping your wine while commenting on the local pointsball team, which reinforces an alibi. As an ST, if a fight broke out in an appropriate context I would allow socialize to continue to apply (after all, a small faux pas like murder doesnt make it suddenly not count). It would also apply to all formal duels.<br /> <br /> In combat you can just read intentions + (with 1000CW) seduce people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T18:03:10-07:00","id":1215291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1215285#post1215285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Definitely, which is probably why it got <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1080152#post1080152\">asked and answered</a> a year ago. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Guess we've been doing it wrong this whole time. Won't change much for the current campaign, which has a couple years to it, but I will keep that in mind for the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T01:11:19-07:00","id":1215398,"title":"","content":"Hmm, just noticed that Blithe Unruffled Plumage from White Veil has a very interesting exception clause:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This includes bonuses to her Guile from White Veil Form or other effects </div> </div> </div>.<br /> <br /> Which means that all the Guile boosters in Socialize apply to it. Well, more than enough reason to take them, even if they don't apply to DED.<br /> <br /> Edit: Hmm Foe Vaulting Method might be useful for activating White Veil Form in combat. I'm going to ask Vance if you can combine it with Birdsong Over Blades to keep your initiative if you deal no damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 05-05-2018, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T08:25:03-07:00","id":1215502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1215398#post1215398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, just noticed that Blithe Unruffled Plumage from White Veil has a very interesting exception clause:<br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> Which means that all the Guile boosters in Socialize apply to it. Well, more than enough reason to take them, even if they don't apply to DED.<br /> <br /> Edit: Hmm Foe Vaulting Method might be useful for activating White Veil Form in combat. I'm going to ask Vance if you can combine it with Birdsong Over Blades to keep your initiative if you deal no damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blinded by laughter also has that clause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T08:58:37-07:00","id":1215514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1215502#post1215502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Blinded by laughter also has that clause.</div> </div> </div> </div>No go on Foe Vaulting Method (ah well).<br /> <br /> Yeah, about Blinded by laughter, I had a couple of questions about that.<br /> <br /> 1. Can you just use it as a Join Battle roll? Say John Q Shikari runs you down in the street, you just declare Blinded by Laughter -&gt; Manipulation + Socialize beats their Resolve -&gt; You join battle and make an Ambush = Profit?<br /> <br /> 2. If you do manage to hit your socially surprised foe, can you reflexively activate White Veil Form before entering the damage determination phase? (Not major, but just wanted to know)<br /> <br /> I've been pondering whats the best way to start a fight for the Black Claw/White Veil Stylist? Is it:<br /> <br /> 1. Regular join battle (Wits + Awareness) which you aren't great at, but you can use Torn Lotus Defense to ambush. Con: If you are Ambushed yourself, it could be pretty bad.<br /> 2. Blinded by Laughter gambit (Manipulation + Socialize) to Ambush. Con: Can you respond to hostilities with it, or do you always have to initiate?<br /> 3. Blinding Battle Feint (Dexterity + Stealth), massive, cheap dice pool, especially with the Belt of Shadow Walking. Con: Quite obvious you are the one initiating hostilities here, how does that play with the audience at home?<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T09:32:03-07:00","id":1215527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1215514#post1215514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No go on Foe Vaulting Method (ah well).<br /> <br /> Yeah, about Blinded by laughter, I had a couple of questions about that.<br /> <br /> 1. Can you just use it as a Join Battle roll? Say John Q Shikari runs you down in the street, you just declare Blinded by Laughter -&gt; Manipulation + Socialize beats their Resolve -&gt; You join battle and make an Ambush = Profit?<br /> <br /> 2. If you do manage to hit your socially surprised foe, can you reflexively activate White Veil Form before entering the damage determination phase? (Not major, but just wanted to know)<br /> <br /> I've been pondering whats the best way to start a fight for the Black Claw/White Veil Stylist? Is it:<br /> <br /> 1. Regular join battle (Wits + Awareness) which you aren't great at, but you can use Torn Lotus Defense to ambush. Con: If you are Ambushed yourself, it could be pretty bad.<br /> 2. Blinded by Laughter gambit (Manipulation + Socialize) to Ambush. Con: Can you respond to hostilities with it, or do you always have to initiate?<br /> 3. Blinding Battle Feint (Dexterity + Stealth), massive, cheap dice pool, especially with the Belt of Shadow Walking. Con: Quite obvious you are the one initiating hostilities here, how does that play with the audience at home?<br /> <br /> prototype00</div> </div> </div> </div>Vance's response only said you wouldn't automatically reset Foe-Vaulting Method by keeping your Initiative. I think you were thinking of one thing here and asked a different thing over there. As it stands, you can indeed activate White Veil Form reflexively by using Foe-Vaulting Method, you just have to dump your Initiative to Base and build it to 6+ before you use Foe-Vaulting Method again.<br /> <br /> 1. I don't think it would work that way. First thing that happens in battle is Join Battle, so you would have to do that before Blinded by Laughter, Blinded by Laughter just substitutes the Stealth component by Socialize.<br /> <br /> 2. It says when you land, so a straight read says yes.<br /> <br /> 1.What you can do to get a more favorable Join Battle, if you are in control of when things go down, is activate White Veil Form before creating a fuss that will cause the Join Battle rolls to happen. So enemies will use Perception + (Lower of Awareness or Socialize), quite possibly crippling many Alpha Strike or any other Awareness dependent builds.<br /> <br /> 2.If they are aware they are in a battle, even if they aren't aware you are an attacker, then you can't Ambush. So no responding to hostilities with an Ambush, but it would still be a Surprise Attack though.<br /> <br /> 3.If you're going Stealth it is better to start the battle already stealthed, (and I would still let you use Blinding Battle Feint anyways) but yeah if you're caught in the open and you're a Stealth build, then Blinding Battle Feint is the way to go.<br /> <br /> And I don't see it being obvious you initiated any hostilities by joining battle with BBF, the perception of who initiated battle is as much a roleplay thing, as a social influence roll with many targets depending on the table, not a function of who wins Join Battle.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T10:36:11-07:00","id":1215546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1215527#post1215527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vance's response only said you wouldn't automatically reset Foe-Vaulting Method by keeping your Initiative. I think you were thinking of one thing here and asked a different thing over there. As it stands, you can indeed activate White Veil Form reflexively by using Foe-Vaulting Method, you just have to dump your Initiative to Base and build it to 6+ before you use Foe-Vaulting Method again.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no, its quite clear. I know that Foe Vaulting Method explicitly allows you to activate White Veil Form if it hits, no confusion there. I'm still trying to find out what happens if your base initiative s &gt;6? We'll see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. I don't think it would work that way. First thing that happens in battle is Join Battle, so you would have to do that before Blinded by Laughter, Blinded by Laughter just substitutes the Stealth component by Socialize. </div> </div> </div>It replaces both the Stealth roll and the Join battle roll, which is where the confusion comes from. If someone wants to fight you (like the Wyld Hunt Shikari I mentioned), can you use Blinded by Laughter to *These aren't the Droids you are looking for* and then Ambush him, is basically what I was asking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. It says when you land, so a straight read says yes. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, thats what I was thinking too, since damage resolution is a separate roll from to hit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1.What you can do to get a more favorable Join Battle, if you are in control of when things go down, is activate White Veil Form before creating a fuss that will cause the Join Battle rolls to happen. So enemies will use Perception + (Lower of Awareness or Socialize), quite possibly crippling many Alpha Strike or any other Awareness dependent builds. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, so that is basically option 2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2.If they are aware they are in a battle, even if they aren't aware you are an attacker, then you can't Ambush. So no responding to hostilities with an Ambush, but it would still be a Surprise Attack though. </div> </div> </div>Ah, here I think you are slightly mistaken. They can be aware that hostilities have started, they just can't be aware of your presence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An ambush is defined as an attack against a target completely<br /> unaware of the attacker\u2019s presence\u2014generally only<br /> possible during the first round of a fight, against a target<br /> with a lower Initiative value than the attacker. An ambush<br /> attack completely ignores the target\u2019s Defense; the target<br /> is considered to have Defense 0 against the attack </div> </div> </div>If you successfully stealthed with Blinding battle feint/Put them off guard with Blinded by Laughter/Faked them out with Open Palm Carress, then you get to Ambush them, even if they saw the fight coming.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to figure out is which of the three approaches to use, since you have to decide at the Join Battle phase, before dice hit the table, and they have different requirements, so activating them all together is not tenable, and even if it was, the mote cost is in no way efficient.<br /> <br /> I suppose if you can't see the attacker then probably default to Blinding Battle Feint. If you can see them, but they are already running up to strike you, then Open Palm Carress and hope they miss their first hit. If you have an opportunity to talk, you can hit them with the Blinded by Laughter Whammy, and then gut them...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T14:20:47-07:00","id":1215591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1215546#post1215546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, no, its quite clear. I know that Foe Vaulting Method explicitly allows you to activate White Veil Form if it hits, no confusion there. I'm still trying to find out what happens if your base initiative s &gt;6? We'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in your post here you questioned whether BOB works with FVM, and on the Ask the Devs you asked if BOB was basically a auto reset for FVM, which Vance said no.<br /> <br /> So yes you can use BOB+FVM and keep your initiative, it only does nothing to reset FVM.<br /> <br /> I just said that to reset FVM you have to dump Initiative to Base and then rebuild it to 6+.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1215546#post1215546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It replaces both the Stealth roll and the Join battle roll, which is where the confusion comes from. If someone wants to fight you (like the Wyld Hunt Shikari I mentioned), can you use Blinded by Laughter to *These aren't the Droids you are looking for* and then Ambush him, is basically what I was asking.</div> </div> </div> </div>It says that you roll Manipulation+Socialize and if it beats the target's Resolve it is an Unexpected Attack, if this result beats their Join Battle result, then it is also an Ambush, if not it is a Surprise Attack. It is a Simple Type Charm, for it to be even used Join Battle has already to have passed. It replaces your Join Battle for a new value for the attack, but it doesn't keep you from having to make the roll on the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1215546#post1215546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, thats what I was thinking too, since damage resolution is a separate roll from to hit.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1215546#post1215546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, so that is basically option 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand what you mean, I talked about activating WVF before battle to possibly lower opponent's Join Battle and keep them from using Awareness Charms if they have lower Socialize. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1215546#post1215546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, here I think you are slightly mistaken. They can be aware that hostilities have started, they just can't be aware of your presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;An ambush is defined as an attack against a target completely<br /> unaware of the attacker\u2019s presence\u2014generally only<br /> possible during the first round of a fight, against a target<br /> with a lower Initiative value than the attacker. An ambush<br /> attack completely ignores the target\u2019s Defense; the target<br /> is considered to have Defense 0 against the attack.<br /> <b>A surprise attack, on the other hand, is an attack launched<br /> from hiding against an opponent who knows he\u2019s in battle<br /> and who is actively on the lookout for attacks, even if he<br /> isn\u2019t sure exactly where all of his opponents are at the<br /> moment.</b> A target faced with a surprise attack suffers a -2<br /> Defense penalty against that attack.&quot;<br /> <br /> You see, I thought in similar lines to what you seem to be, too. But when I asked Vance about why a stealthed BOB user wouldn't be able to just keep ambush BOBing people from stealth, he just said no, but didn't seem to want to go further into it on why. So I'm trying to make sense of why a completely unknown attacker who performed a completely unnoticeable attack is no longer capable of an ambush.<br /> <br /> And this is the way I found to reconcile this.<br /> <br /> So if the opponent knows something is up, even if they don't know about you or where you are, it is a surprise attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1215546#post1215546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you successfully stealthed with Blinding battle feint/Put them off guard with Blinded by Laughter/Faked them out with Open Palm Carress, then you get to Ambush them, even if they saw the fight coming.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to figure out is which of the three approaches to use, since you have to decide at the Join Battle phase, before dice hit the table, and they have different requirements, so activating them all together is not tenable, and even if it was, the mote cost is in no way efficient.<br /> <br /> I suppose if you can't see the attacker then probably default to Blinding Battle Feint. If you can see them, but they are already running up to strike you, then Open Palm Carress and hope they miss their first hit. If you have an opportunity to talk, you can hit them with the Blinded by Laughter Whammy, and then gut them...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are mistaking the exception based power of specific Charms, with the general rules.<br /> <br /> If they see you and then you disappear by joining battle with BBF, you can't ambush them anymore, only surprise attack them.<br /> <br /> If they are aware of the situation you can only ambush them with OPC, BbL or Mind Shroud Meditation, (but this only after Shadow Victor's Repose extra join battles, not the original one).<br /> <br /> So if you want to open with an ambush, you have 3 options, OPC, BbL or start the battle already stealthed and basically win join battle, <br /> <br /> P.S. I think MSM also supports the &quot;unaware of you&quot; interpretation, since it lets you ambush by making people forget about you for a bit. I will try again with Vance to see what he says.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T20:59:58-07:00","id":1215980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1215941#post1215941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Veil Form isn't really relevant; it only mitigates flurry penalties, and you can't flurry two influence rolls together with each other.<br /> <br /> Poised Lion Attitude lets you make a Presence or Socialize-based influence roll reflexively on your turn. Whether that's in addition to an influence roll made using your normal action isn't specified; I'd personally be against it unless there's a good stunt other than &quot;I say these two things really fast.&quot;<br /> <br /> Thousand Courtesan Ways lets you tag seduction-based influence onto the back of another social roll. You could use it together with Poised Lion Attitude, although I don't think mid-combat seduction would be super effective.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1215941#post1215941\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1215941#post1215941\"> Ask the Devs - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1215941#post1215941\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1215941#post1215941 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Dear Exalted fans, as you may be aware from the latest Onyx Path Monday Meeting notes (http://theonyxpath.com/princes-gambit-joy-exalted-plans-monday-meeting-notes/), Robert Vance and I have been honored with the opportunity to take on line editor duties for Exalted Third Edition. As part of that, we want to make ourselves available to the community as a resource to keep you informed as best we can about the line. Obviously there will be some questions we can't answer! But when we're not working on upcoming books, we'll drop in to touch base. We'll be using this thread as our port of call so that we </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So, probably a no-go on four social actions at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T21:07:04-07:00","id":1215981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1215980#post1215980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1215941#post1215941\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...41#post1215941</a><br /> <br /> So, probably a no-go on four social actions at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, more like you\u2019d have to stunt it with a good stunt, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T05:31:38-07:00","id":1216057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1214924#post1214924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...<br /> <br /> Of course you gotta roleplay the hell out of this interaction, but it is mechanically possible. I think. LOL.<br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that whole deal had this caveat since the beginning, in my view anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T08:01:38-07:00","id":1216126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1216057#post1216057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that whole deal had this caveat since the beginning, in my view anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>True dat. Besides, unless you're going whole hog in trying to make your opponent your mind controlled puppet, I find one or two positive instills is more than enough to make them regret life (hence why my Dawn Black Claw chose charms quite differently from my Eclipse Black Claw).<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T08:07:13-07:00","id":1216131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212902-synergys-of-the-black-veiled-courtesan?p=1216126#post1216126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True dat. Besides, unless you're going whole hog in trying to make your opponent your mind controlled puppet, I find one or two positive instills is more than enough to make them regret life (hence why my Dawn Black Claw chose charms quite differently from my Eclipse Black Claw).<br /> <br /> prototype00</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, unless your objective is to make a puppet out of an attacker in a few rounds, it is going overboard. You don't need all that for it to be functional, it was just taking it to the limit for science's sake!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}